      "side": 1,
      "message": "That one was more or less perfect for the native stack!\n\nWhen I was still fishing for the root cause of my issue, I was trying to see what events the Java stack was getting from native so I could work backwards. The type of debugging I added in this change helps do that. I didn\u0027t add any log lines. I just added the obfuscated MAC address to most of them so you can actually tell which device they belong to.\n\nI also added a class of device section to dumpsys so you can quickly tell what we think the class of device is/ultimately what we\u0027re sending out `BluetoothDevice#getBluetoothClass()`, i.e.:\n```\nBonded devices:\n    AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF [ DUAL ][ 0x001F00 ] Pixel 6 Pro\n```\n\nI figured it might be useful in something like LE Audio debugging too where we\u0027re curious if the remote device has the proper bits set in its class of device.",
